  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kajiado Pastoralists&apos; Integrated Food Security Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to contribute towards food security and resilience for poor and vulnerable communities in Ewasu and Torosei locations of Kajiado County, Kenya. It seeks to improve: 
&#x2022; income and livestock production levels, through training in financial and business management, and training in value addition on milk products, brick making for youths, goat distribution to special groups and water bottling for youth groups;   
&#x2022; community access to water for both human and livestock use and safe sanitation and hygiene practices. This will be achieved through rehabilitation of water pans, construction of sanitation facilities and through hygiene promotion activities;
&#x2022; disaster management and preparedness, and sustainable management of natural resources, through training and vulnerability assessments;
&#x2022; advocacy for the target communities, through the identification of key advocacy issues and appropriate training and awareness campaigns

The project will seek to collaborate with the private sector and relevant government institutions both at the county and national level.</narrative>
  </description>
